# 1. STRICT PROJECT REQUIREMENTS

Follow these requirements throughout the entire project.

### Database and API restrictions

- Do NOT use any database.
- Do NOT use MongoDB.
- Do NOT use Firebase.
- Do NOT use Supabase.
- Do NOT use PostgreSQL.
- Do NOT use MySQL.
- Do NOT use any external database service.
- Do NOT use any API keys.
- Do NOT use OpenAI APIs.
- Do NOT use Gemini APIs.
- Do NOT use external AI APIs.
- Do NOT require API authentication.
- Do NOT require paid third-party services.
- Do NOT require cloud storage.
- Do NOT require external video hosting.

Everything must work locally within the browser.

Use:
- React state.
- Zustand or Context API.
- LocalStorage for small application preferences and settings.
- IndexedDB for optional locally persisted user data and video blobs.
- Browser File API for video uploads.
- URL.createObjectURL for local video playback.
- Three.js for 3D rendering.
- Web Audio API for audio processing.

Do not store large video files in LocalStorage.

Video files must remain local to the browser unless the user explicitly downloads or exports them.

No login or signup pages.

No payment gateway.

No subscription system.

No fake backend.

No mock API responses.

Do not show fake upload progress or pretend files have been uploaded when they have not.

### Main requirement

Every feature must be genuinely interactive and functional.

Do not create a website that only looks good in screenshots.

